33,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Minato,,The treasurer spent six hours a month chasing individual payments.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, like hall hire.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,Nine people who didn't join said they couldn't commit to a whole year.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,Turnout dropped by a third after we tried charging per event.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,The same nine people do the setup and are the top attendees.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if costs are fixed, why do we chase individual payments?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,Because the bank statements show a third of renewals need reminders.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,The quiet members are uneasy about what their two visits cost.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,People stopped treating the evenings as theirs when we charged per door.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,The sign-in sheets show a quarter of members do two-thirds of the work.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,Chasing money is too much work. We need a simpler way.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,Fixed costs mean we need reliable income. A flat fee might work.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"If we make it too visible, people will feel judged.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"Activity-based charging made people feel like guests, not members.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"If we charge per event, the heavy users pay more, but the light users might leave.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I am leaning towards a flat fee to reduce the admin burden.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,A flat fee covers the fixed costs without constant chasing.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,But will it feel fair to those who come rarely?,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,It feels safer. People know what they owe at the start.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,It is the simplest. Let us see if the others agree.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
