59,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option A is a flat annual fee. It covers everything.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option B is activity-based. You pay for what you use.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option C is tiered. You choose a level of participation.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,I remember how bad Option B felt. It created distance.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option C might be too complicated. We had friction with grades before.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, does the flat fee cover the fixed costs you found?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,Yes. The hall and insurance are fixed. A flat fee is predictable.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,The taster forms showed people don't want a whole year commitment.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,But they also don't want to pay per event. It's a dilemma.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,The flat fee is the least work for the treasurer.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,I vote for A. It is the most sustainable for the admin.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. A is the most rational choice for our finances.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I am worried about the newcomers, but A is the safest.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"I prefer A. It feels like belonging, not transacting.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,A is the only one that doesn't create new problems.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,It seems we are all leaning towards A.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,The data supports it. Let us proceed.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,"I will support A, but we must be gentle with the communication.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"Yes. Let's make it feel like a community, not a bill.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,Agreed. Let's vote.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
